{"step_index":366,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:40:16Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. kita lanjut ke fitur selanjutnya kira kira apa ya dan udahberapa persen\n2. iya opsi 1\n3. Bibi AI Error: Error [ApiError]: {\"error\":{\"code\":404,\"message\":\"This model models/gemini-2.5-flash is no longer available to new users. Please update your code to use models/gemini-3.8-flash for the latest features and improvements. We recommend you to use \r\nthe Interactions API (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/get-started).\",\"status\":\"NOT_FOUND\"}}\r\n    at async POST (src\\app\\api\\bibi\\route.ts:65:22)\r\n  63 | ...\r\n  64 | ...\r\n> 65 | ...nst response = await ai.models...     |                   ^\r\n  66 | ...model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",       \r\n  67 | ...contents: [\r\n  68 | ...  { role: \"system\", parts: [{ ... {\r\n  status: 404\r\n}\r\n POST /api/bibi 500 in 3.2s (next.js: 1201ms, application-code: 1956ms)\r\n\n4. itu yang level ke 3 belum kebuka padahal saya sudah menyelesaikan level 2\n5. tolong level 3 perbaiki itu buat user bingung\n6. gak bisa di seret\n7. bisa dibuat lebih simpel gak dari level 3 itu anak kecil bisa bingung \n8. oke, selanjutnya tolong icon atas itu diganti ya, disitu masih logo next .js\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: Change the top icon (\"icon atas\"), which currently still displays the default Next.js logo.\n- **Context & Scope**: In Next.js App Router, when no custom favicon or app icon exists in `src/app/` or `public/`, the browser tab displays the default Next.js triangular logo. The user requested replacing this with the custom branded CodeKids icon.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Earlier Turns**:\n  - **Game-Loop & Rewards**: Implemented dynamic victory modal, Web Audio API sound effects (`src/lib/audio.ts`), confetti (`src/components/ui/Confetti.tsx`), and badge col\n<truncated 1162 bytes>\n- **Brand Identity**: The CodeKids icon in `src/components/brand/Logo.tsx` uses a rounded squircle badge in bright orange (`#FF8A2B`) containing the code symbol `</>` in bold white text.\n- **Next.js App Router Icon Convention**:\n  - Placing `src/app/icon.svg` (or `src/app/icon.tsx` / `public/favicon.ico`) with type `image/svg+xml` will automatically generate and serve the browser tab favicon across all pages.\n  - Updating `icons` in `export const metadata: Metadata` inside `src/app/layout.tsx` guarantees browser pickup and manifest consistency.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Workspace**: `e:\\codekids`\n- **Environment**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, Prisma SQLite.\n- **Target Files for Icon**:\n  - `src/app/icon.svg` (primary high-res vector icon).\n  - `public/favicon.ico` / `public/icon.svg`.\n  - `src/app/layout.tsx` (metadata icon link).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Create `src/app/icon.svg`**:\n   - Create SVG with viewBox `0 0 32 32`.\n   - Render rounded rectangle (`rx=\"8\"`, fill `#FF8A2B`) and white centered code brackets `</>` with playful typography matching the brand.\n2. **Add `public/favicon.ico` / `public/icon.svg`**:\n   - Provide standard favicon fallback for direct `/favicon.ico` requests.\n3. **Update `metadata` in `src/app/layout.tsx`**:\n   - Add `icons: { icon: \"/icon.svg\" }` or let Next.js auto-detect `src/app/icon.svg`.\n4. **Verify**:\n   - Check that the browser tab displays the custom orange CodeKids `</>` icon instead of the Next.js logo.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must match the brand color scheme: `#FF8A2B` (orange), `#1B2A5C` (navy), and clean white text.\n- Do not introduce heavy dependencies or binary image files that could fail to render.\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`","truncated_fields":["content"]}
